A||||3||Raydar||Computer problem solved. W2K/Word 97 error.||||10||
Z||000000||Raydar||08-06-2001||01:45 PM||||Okay, I've had this problem for <I>months</I>... Until Saturday.<BR>Running W2K. When opening MSWord 97, after about 10 seconds I would see a pop-up, "Winword.exe has generated errors and will be shut down. An error log is being generated".<BR>Then the app would close. <BR>Long story short. I was using an OfficeJet printer that was connected to my wife's computer, and shared across our network. When her computer was off, Word couldn't find the default printer and freaked out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><BR>What a POS Application/OS!!!  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000001||theogre||08-06-2001||08:43 PM||||Printing in Windows has never been very stable. It's one of the top 10 support problems we have at work.<P>Office programs use the printer driver at all times. The first thing they do on startup is try to get page layout info from them.<P>If you are tight on system resources the item most likely to set it off will be a print function.<P>Also make sure you have the most recent driver. The ones that come with stuff are often way out dated.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 08-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-07-2001||12:42 AM||||Thanks for the tips. <BR>Really freakish thing is that it used to blow up "Notepad", too. <BR>...another Microsoft feature. <P>Glad I went to Telecomm. Computers suck, much of the time.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||SteveJ||08-07-2001||10:51 AM||||Computers are an unperfected technology.<P>It's kind of like driving a car in 1910.||||reg||1
